%N A397899 a(n) is the smallest number k such that 2*(k-n) = sigma(k) - n*tau(k).
%H A397899 Žiga Pirc, <a href="/A397899/b397899.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..100</a>
%e A397899 a(2) = 24, since sigma(24) - 2*tau(24) = 60 - 16 = 44 = 2*(24-2).
%o A397899 (PARI) A397899(n) = my(k=1); while(2*(k-n) != sigma(k) - n*numdiv(k), k++); return(k);
